- [Expo](https://expo.dev/) SDK 57, [React Native](https://reactnative.dev/),
  and npm packages in `mobile/app/package.json` — each keeps its own license.
  `node_modules/` is not committed.
- `react-native-ble-manager` and other native modules: see their upstream repos.
- Apple Watch app uses Apple watchOS / Swift / SwiftUI. Those SDKs are not
  redistributed here. Bundle IDs and `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` in `project.yml` /
  `app.json` are the maintainer’s; forks must replace them.

## Integrations (not vendored)

- XiaoZhi official MCP pipe sample: [78/mcp-calculator](https://github.com/78/mcp-calculator) — clone separately.
- Python package `mcp` (see `integrations/xiaozhi-mcp/requirements.txt`) — install into a local venv.
- [UlanziDeckPlugin-SDK](https://github.com/UlanziTechnology/UlanziDeckPlugin-SDK) — required to package the D200H plugin; not copied into this tree.
- `ws` (Ulanzi plugin `package.json`) — MIT; install with npm when packaging.
- Karabiner-Elements and GoatRemote are host apps the user installs; this repo only ships config / prompt extras.

## Protocol / product inspiration

- [Upsy Desky](https://github.com/tjhorner/upsy-desky) — open standing-desk bridge concepts (UART-oriented). Desk Gateway uses a different physical/protocol path (I²C panel emulation / MITM) for the desks documented here.

## Optional tooling (not vendored)

- Protocol capture: **[nanoDLA](https://github.com/wuxx/nanoDLA)** (open-source FX2 logic analyzer; PulseView / `fx2lafw`). Not required to build firmware.

